 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "They can be restrictive and don't always facilitate the best ideas.",
  "So, my advice is simple: never use a whiteboard for brainstorming.",
  "There are far more effective methods we can employ.",
  "Now, when it comes to your coding practices, I'd like you to follow a specific convention for function argument names.",
  "Always start them with 'h_'.",
  "This is a style I've found immensely useful for maintaining clean and consistent code.",
  "I'm a strong advocate for establishing good habits early on.",
  "It might take some time to adjust, but I assure you, these practices will benefit you and the team in the long run.",
  "Now, as you settle into your new role, feel free to reach out to me with any questions or concerns.",
  "My door is always open, and I'm here to support your growth and development.",
  "Please do, and don't hesitate to connect with your colleagues across the company.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you need anything at all.",
  "So, moving forward, I want you to start following a new convention for function argument names and variable names.",
  "For function arguments, start the name with 'i_'.",
  "And for variable names, end them with '_m'.",
  "This will help us maintain consistency and improve code readability across the team.",
  "Well, we've discussed this with the team leads, and we believe that establishing clear and unique naming conventions will reduce confusion, especially when multiple engineers are working on the same project.",
  "It's all about making our code more maintainable and understandable for everyone involved."
 ],
